# Testing

## Stack

- Runner: Vitest (`npm test` → `vitest --ui`)
- Environment: `happy-dom`
- DOM assertions: `@testing-library/jest-dom/vitest` (configured in `vitest.setup.ts`)
- Component testing: `@testing-library/react` + `@testing-library/user-event`
- Globals: `describe`, `it`, `expect`, `vi` available without imports (but import explicitly for clarity)

## File Placement

- UI primitives: colocate `{name}.test.tsx` next to `{name}.tsx`
- Form fields: `src/components/form/fields/__tests__/{name}.test.tsx`

## Test Structure

```tsx
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import userEvent from "@testing-library/user-event";
import { describe, expect, it, vi } from "vitest";

describe("Button", () => {
  it("calls onClick", async () => {
    const user = userEvent.setup();
    const onClick = vi.fn();
    render(<Button onClick={onClick}>Save</Button>);
    await user.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Save" }));
    expect(onClick).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
  });
});
```

## Conventions

- Query by role/label/text — avoid `container.querySelector` and test IDs unless testing icons
- Use `userEvent.setup()` for interactions (not `fireEvent`)
- Use `vi.fn()` for callbacks, `vi.mock()` sparingly
- Form field tests: wrap in `UiForm` or `FormProvider` with a minimal Zod schema
- Test behavior and accessibility — not implementation details or CSS class names
- One `describe` block per component, multiple focused `it` blocks

## Path Alias

`@/` resolves to `src/` in tests (configured in `vitest.config.mts`).

## Refusals

- Do NOT use Jest — this project uses Vitest only.
- Do NOT add Playwright/Cypress unless explicitly requested.
- Do NOT snapshot entire component trees — prefer semantic queries.
- Do NOT skip tests for new UI primitives or form fields.
